-**Formulas:**
-* Opacity/conic test (baseline): $\alpha_g = \text{opacity}_g \cdot \exp(-\frac{1}{2} \mathbf{d}^T \Sigma^{-1} \mathbf{d})$ [S1]
-* Alpha compositing update: $C_p \leftarrow C_p + \alpha_g \cdot T_p \cdot \text{color}_g$ [S1]
-* Transmittance update: $T_p \leftarrow T_p \cdot (1 - \alpha_g)$ [S1]
+**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
+*   **Bin Order:** Entries within a bin are not depth-sorted unless selective exact repair has restored the order. The method relies on the concatenation of bins being in front-to-back bin order, not necessarily within each bin [S1].
+*   **Precision:** Standard floating-point precision is used for accumulators. Early termination thresholds must be chosen carefully to avoid visual artifacts from premature culling.
+*   **Boundaries:** The scan interval $[a, b)$ is exclusive of $b$. Ensure `binOffsets` array is sized correctly to avoid out-of-bounds access.
 
-**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-* The linear scan processes unsorted intra-bin entries in batch order, which is acceptable because the front-to-back bin layout ensures correct compositing across bins [S1].
-* Selective exact repair restores exact baseline depth order within bins when needed, but does not handle cross-bin ordering as the bin layout already guarantees front-to-back progression [S1].
-* The early-termination threshold for $T_p$ is a configurable parameter [S1].
+## Subtopics
